  "source_texts": [
    "The Birth of __PERSON_F__\n1 In those days Caesar Augustus issued a decree that a census should be taken of the entire Roman world. 2 (This was the first census that took place while[a] Quirinius was governor of Syria.) 3 And everyone went to their own town to register.\n\n4 So __PERSON_E__ also went up from the town of __VILLAGE_A__ in __REGION_A__ to Judea, to Bethlehem the town of __KING_A__, because he belonged to the house and line of __KING_A__. 5 He went there to register with __PERSON_D__, who was pledged to be married to him and was expecting a child. 6 While they were there, the time came for the baby to be born, 7 and she gave birth to her firstborn, a son. She wrapped him in cloths and placed him in a manger, because there was no guest room available for them.\n\n8 And there were shepherds living out in the fields nearby, keeping watch over their flocks at night. 9 An angel of the __MASTER_A__ appeared to them, and the glory of the __MASTER_A__ shone around them, and they were terrified. 10 But the angel said to them, “Do not be afraid. I bring you good news that will cause great joy for all the people. 11 Today in the town of __KING_A__ a Savior has been born to you; he is the Messiah, the __MASTER_A__. 12 This will be a sign to you: You will find a baby wrapped in cloths and lying in a manger.”\n\n13 Suddenly a great company of the heavenly host appeared with the angel, praising __MOST_HIGH_A__ and saying,\n\n14 “Glory to __MOST_HIGH_A__ in the highest heaven,\n    and on earth peace to those on whom his favor rests.”\n\n15 When the angels had left them and gone into heaven, the shepherds said to one another, “Let’s go to Bethlehem and see this thing that has happened, which the __MASTER_A__ has told us about.”\n\n16 So they hurried off and found __PERSON_D__ and __PERSON_E__, and the baby, who was lying in the manger. 17 When they had seen him, they spread the word concerning what had been told them about this child, 18 and all who heard it were amazed at what the shepherds said to them. 19 But __PERSON_D__ treasured up all these things and pondered them in her heart. 20 The shepherds returned, glorifying and praising __MOST_HIGH_A__ for all the things they had heard and seen, which were just as they had been told.\n\n21 On the eighth day, when it was time to circumcise the child, he was named __PERSON_F__, the name the angel had given him before he was conceived.\n\n__PERSON_F__ Presented in the Temple\n22 When the time came for the purification rites required by the Law of Moses, __PERSON_E__ and __PERSON_D__ took him to __CITY_A__ to present him to the __MASTER_A__ 23 (as it is written in the Law of the __MASTER_A__, “Every firstborn male is to be consecrated to the __MASTER_A__”[b]), 24 and to offer a sacrifice in keeping with what is said in the Law of the __MASTER_A__: “a pair of doves or two young pigeons.”[c]\n\n25 Now there was a man in __CITY_A__ called Simeon, who was righteous and devout. He was waiting for the consolation of __PEOPLE_A__, and the __SPIRIT_A__ was on him. 26 It had been revealed to him by the __SPIRIT_A__ that he would not die before he had seen the __MASTER_A__ Messiah. 27 Moved by the Spirit, he went into the __PLACE_A__ courts. When the parents brought in the child __PERSON_F__ to do for him what the custom of the Law required, 28 Simeon took him in his arms and praised __MOST_HIGH_A__, saying:\n\n29 “Sovereign __MASTER_A__, as you have promised,\n    you may now dismiss[d] your servant in peace.\n30 For my eyes have seen your salvation,\n31     which you have prepared in the sight of all nations:\n32 a light for revelation to the Gentiles,\n    and the glory of your people __PEOPLE_A__.”\n\n33 The child’s father and mother marveled at what was said about him. 34 Then Simeon blessed them and said to __PERSON_D__, his mother: “This child is destined to cause the falling and rising of many in __PEOPLE_A__, and to be a sign that will be spoken against, 35 so that the thoughts of many hearts will be revealed. And a sword will pierce your own soul too.”\n\n36 There was also a prophet, Anna, the daughter of Penuel, of the tribe of Asher. She was very old; she had lived with her husband seven years after her marriage, 37 and then was a widow until she was eighty-four.[e] She never left the __PLACE_A__ but worshiped night and day, fasting and __REQUEST_A__. 38 Coming up to them at that very moment, she gave thanks to __MOST_HIGH_A__ and spoke about the child to all who were looking forward to the redemption of __CITY_A__.\n\n39 When __PERSON_E__ and __PERSON_D__ had done everything required by the Law of the __MASTER_A__, they returned to __REGION_A__ to their own town of __VILLAGE_A__. 40 And the child grew and became strong; he was filled with wisdom, and the grace of __MOST_HIGH_A__ was on him.\n\nThe Boy __PERSON_F__ at the Temple\n41 Every year __PERSON_F__ parents went to __CITY_A__ for the Festival of the Passover. 42 When he was twelve years old, they went up to the festival, according to the custom. 43 After the festival was over, while his parents were returning home, the boy __PERSON_F__ stayed behind in __CITY_A__, but they were unaware of it. 44 Thinking he was in their company, they traveled on for a day. Then they began looking for him among their relatives and friends. 45 When they did not find him, they went back to __CITY_A__ to look for him. 46 After three days they found him in the __PLACE_A__ courts, sitting among the teachers, listening to them and asking them questions. 47 Everyone who heard him was amazed at his understanding and his answers. 48 When his parents saw him, they were astonished. His mother said to him, “Son, why have you treated us like this? Your father and I have been anxiously searching for you.”\n\n49 “Why were you searching for me?” he asked. “Didn’t you know I had to be in my Father’s house?”[f] 50 But they did not understand what he was saying to them.\n\n51 Then he went down to __VILLAGE_A__ with them and was obedient to them. But his mother treasured all these things in her heart. 52 And __PERSON_F__ grew in wisdom and stature, and in favor with __MOST_HIGH_A__ and man.\n\n"
  ],
  "translations": [
    "__PERSON_F__的诞生  \n1 当那些日子，凯撒·奥古斯都颁布诏令，要为全罗马帝国进行人口普查。2 （这是基里尼乌斯任叙利亚省长时进行的第一次人口普查。）3 众人各归各城登记。  \n\n4 于是，__PERSON_E__也从属于__REGION_A__的__VILLAGE_A__城上犹太，到了属于__KING_A__家的伯利恒城，因为他是__KING_A__家族和血统的人。5 他同有婚约、怀孕的未婚妻__PERSON_D__一同去那里登记。6 他们在那里时，孩子到了出生的日期，7 她生了头胎的儿子，用布包裹，放在马槽里，因为客店里没有空房。  \n\n8 当时，在附近的田野有牧羊人夜间看守羊群。9 __MASTER_A__的一位天使向他们显现，主的荣耀环绕他们，他们十分惧怕。10 天使对他们说：“不要害怕。我报给你们大喜的信息，是关乎普天下人的。11 今天在__KING_A__城里，为你们生了救主，就是__MASTER_A__所立的基督。12 你们要认得这兆头：你们必发现包着布，卧在马槽里的婴孩。”  \n\n13 忽然，有一大队天兵与天使一同赞美__MOST_HIGH_A__说，  \n\n14 “在至高之处荣耀归与__MOST_HIGH_A__，  \n    在地上平安归与他所喜悦的人。”  \n\n15 天使离开他们升天后，牧羊人彼此说：“我们往伯利恒去，看__MASTER_A__告诉我们的这件事。”  \n\n16 他们急忙去了，找到__PERSON_D__和__PERSON_E__，还有躺在马槽里的婴孩。17 见到他后，将天使对他们说的话传开，18 凡听见的人都希奇牧羊人所讲的事。19 __PERSON_D__却把这些事存在心里，反复思量。20 牧羊人回去，归荣耀赞美__MOST_HIGH_A__，因所听见所看见的一切，正如天使所说。  \n\n21 八日，按礼为孩子行割礼，起名叫__PERSON_F__，这是天使怀他以前所起的名字。  \n\n__PERSON_F__在殿里献上  \n22 按摩西律法上所规定洁净的日期到了，__PERSON_E__和__PERSON_D__带他到__CITY_A__，将他献给__MASTER_A__，23 （正如__MASTER_A__律法所记：“凡头生的男孩，要归给__MASTER_A__”[b]），24 并照着__MASTER_A__律法上所说献祭：“一对斑鸠或两只雏鸽。”[c]  \n\n25 当时，在__CITY_A__有一个人，名叫西面，他是个义人，虔诚敬畏神。等待以色列的安慰，且圣灵在他身上。26 圣灵曾向他启示，他未死之前必见到主所立的弥赛亚。27 他被圣灵感动，进了殿内。当父母带着小孩__PERSON_F__来行律法所需的礼节时，28 西面就抱着他，称颂__MOST_HIGH_A__说：  \n\n29 “主啊，按照你的话，  \n    如今可以释放你的仆人安然去世。  \n30 因为我亲眼看见了你的救恩，  \n31 就是你在众民面前所预备的，  \n32 一盏给外邦人启示的光，  \n    是你民以色列的荣耀。”  \n\n33 孩子的父母因所说的这话惊讶。34 西面又给他们祝福，对他母亲__PERSON_D__说：“这个孩子立志要使以色列中的许多人兴衰倒伏，并成为被人反对的兆头，35 叫许多心里的意念显露出来。你的心也要被刀刺透。”  \n\n36 当时，也有女先知亚拿，是亚设支派的比努以勒女儿。她年纪甚大，嫁夫七年，37 丧夫成为寡妇一直活到八十四岁。[e]她不离开殿，昼夜事奉神，禁食祷告。38 忽然来到他们那里，感谢神，并向众等候耶路撒冷得赎回的人述说这孩子。  \n\n39 按律法办完一切事后，__PERSON_E__和__PERSON_D__带孩子回__REGION_A__自己的城__VILLAGE_A__去。40 孩子渐渐增长强壮，充满智慧，并蒙__MOST_HIGH_A__恩典眷顾。  \n\n少年__PERSON_F__在殿中  \n41 每年，__PERSON_F__的父母按惯例往__CITY_A__守逾越节。42 当他十二岁时，他们照例上节期。43 节期完毕归家途中，少年__PERSON_F__仍留在殿中，父母却不知情，44 以为他同行，走了一天路，便寻找亲戚和熟人。45 寻找未果，便回到__CITY_A__找他。46 三天后，他们在殿里找着他，坐在教师中间，一面听，一面问。47 凡听见他的，都诧异他的悟性和回答。48 看见他父母也惊讶。他母亲对他说：“儿子，为什么这样待我们？你父亲和我极力寻你。”  \n\n49 他说：“你们为什么找我？岂不知我应当以我父的事为念吗？”[f]50 他们却不明白所说的话。  \n\n51 他下去与他们同回__VILLAGE_A__，服从他们。他母亲却把这一切事存在心里。52 __PERSON_F__在智慧和身量，以及神和人面前恩宠上，都渐渐长大。"
  ],
